The .node files of the elmdb npm package are compiled from elmdb's Rust code, the Rust standard library, the crates
below and two C libraries they bundle: LMDB, in lmdb-master-sys, and zstd, in zstd-sys. This file holds the license
and notices of each crate, as their licenses require of a binary redistribution: each license names the crates it
covers, with their authors, then gives its text. A few of the crates are procedural macros, and what those use, which
run while the package is compiled and leave no code of their own in it; they are listed with the rest.

Some crates ship no license file, and cargo-about gives their license's standard text, where the copyright line is a
placeholder such as "Copyright (c) <year> <copyright holders>". Such a crate is listed with the authors its manifest
names, or, where it names none, the repository it is from, which holds its history.

`cargo xtask notices` writes this file from the lockfile with cargo-about, and copies the Rust standard library's
notices from the toolchain; `cargo xtask check-notices` fails when either is stale.

